{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789263501,"nonce":"Bk0gHrDeeGF2NXl2xeBcoLZJCkU=","title":"Core typed dispatcher: per-width tables on wasm","message":"The core's default typed dispatcher (LANG_CORE only, up to four arguments)\nunifies the integer-class argument widths into one register slot, which\nholds on SysV x86-64, AAPCS64 and Win64. wasm types every function\nsignature exactly, so an i32 argument and an i64 argument are different\nfunction types and the unified transmute is wrong there. Needs a\nper-width table under cfg(target_family = \"wasm\"). Not reachable until a\ncore callable runs on wasm.","files":null}]}